OL,3,GNEWSASinn Fein 'content' with 1998
OL,4,Abombing campaign, Omagh inquiry told
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe police officer who headed up the
OL,7,FOmagh bomb investigation has told an
OL,8,Finquiry that members of Sinn Fein were
OL,9,F"content" with bombings carried out in
OL,10,F1998.
OL,12,FRetired PSNI Ch Supt Norman Baxter said
OL,13,Fthe bombing campaign of early 1998 "was
OL,14,Fbeneficial in the political
OL,15,Fnegotiations Sinn Fein had with the
OL,16,FBritish government".
OL,18,FThe Omagh Bombing Inquiry is examining
OL,19,Fwhether the attack on 15 August 1998,
OL,20,Fin which 29 people including a woman
OL,21,Fpregnant with twins were killed, could
OL,22,Fhave been prevented.
OL,23,APub: 16-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NI NewsC Reg TVF On This Day
